    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fe853afe-d1fa-364e-818d-252e2ecb041e",
                "word": "uncountably",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                        "entry_id": "fe853afe-d1fa-364e-818d-252e2ecb041e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Too many to be counted (either by reason of being infinite or for practical constraints)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a640e45-2907-4872-b365-5582b01e724e",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "The stars in the sky are uncountably many. Even a lifetime would not suffice to number them all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "411787ea-da58-4587-91ff-227db84009d9",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "And the dimensions of death that can result from such systems tripped in error, or through misperceptions of reality, are uncountably greater than those"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f44fcb52-6216-4fc7-90fd-7287e4ebe912",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "a host of other producers fear that a vital link to New York's uncountably diverse populations is about to be cut."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71dd0734-3af6-4e49-b9ea-c822aa8e3789",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "And the memory of man runneth not to a year when there was an episode of disproportion comparable to the planet-wide vapors occasioned by one of the year's uncountably numerous automobile accidents, this one in Paris."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a385a15a-8e87-4e30-9d55-2e5bfd9d6840",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "and the sheer quantity of material is uncountably greater"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a29b40a-ca44-431b-a011-4f8f313d49b0",
                                "sense_id": "11f74286-c0c3-35fc-8984-dfee50e9fa5f",
                                "text": "Stories of road travel in the United States have taken uncountably many forms, from John Steinbeck's \"Travels With Charley\" and Jack Kerouac's \"On the Road\" to \"Little Miss Sunshine\"."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55bb46cb-f216-34ee-b577-874ba96d432a",
                        "entry_id": "fe853afe-d1fa-364e-818d-252e2ecb041e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In an uncountable fashion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d811974c-3b13-4c2f-b9d6-a323b2c90828",
                                "sense_id": "55bb46cb-f216-34ee-b577-874ba96d432a",
                                "text": "Some nouns can be used both countably and uncountably."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ef22474-ea9e-3ad1-8b4d-333edf6d5480",
                        "entry_id": "fe853afe-d1fa-364e-818d-252e2ecb041e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a way that is incapable of being put into one-to-one correspondence with the natural numbers or any subset thereof."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "025b13fc-a056-4398-b707-dc62fcd8802a",
                                "sense_id": "4ef22474-ea9e-3ad1-8b4d-333edf6d5480",
                                "text": "If a set is neither finite nor countably infinite, it is said to be uncountably infinite or simply uncountable."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
